{"_id":"68a736208ec3d8323af18ab7","nodeId":"IdGdLNgJI3WmONEFsMq-d","roadmapSlug":"ios","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:12.170Z","description":"# Core OS\n\nCore OS is the bottom layer of the iOS architecture, sitting directly above the hardware. It provides the Darwin kernel, security frameworks, and low-level system interfaces. Frameworks at this level include Security, Accelerate for math and signal processing, and ExternalAccessory for communicating with hardware accessories.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Kernel API","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/kernel","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf863a"},{"type":"article","title":"System Configuration","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/systemconfiguration","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf863b"},{"type":"article","title":"Apple File System Guide","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/file_system/about_apple_file_system","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf863c"},{"type":"article","title":"Keychain Services","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/keychain_services","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf863d"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:24.838Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ios/content/IdGdLNgJI3WmONEFsMq-d.md"}